# GREEN.hard — the two hard blocks are parity-green (F6)

Written when the guard (`pre-tool-use-guard`) and the stop gate (`stop-gate`) were
ported to `vibe-flow` and checked against the frozen bash fallbacks.

That is what `port-order` gates on: `crates/vibe-flow/src/tui/` and
`crates/vibe-signals/` may not exist before this file does, because both would be
built on top of enforcement that has not been proven (docs/spec/tech/rust/rust-parity-pins.md).

## Evidence at the freeze

- Port: `crates/vibe-flow/src/hook.rs` — guard, stop, the `decide` fallback with its
  shape gate, and `Command::Hook { event }`; PR #65.
- Parity at that head: flow candidate 505 passed / 5 pinned / 0 failed over 510
  runs, flow self-check 510/510, spec 132 passed / 17 pinned; CI 11/11 green
  including both windows-latest toolchains.
- Shim: `flow/bin/hook.sh` reaches the guard/stop behaviour through five tiers, and
  the last one (`flow/bin/fallback/`) is byte-identical to the frozen oracle, so the
  hard blocks survive a missing binary and a missing node (`flow/tests/hooks.sh`).

Remove this file only when the marker's claim stops being true — i.e. never for
convenience; a red guard/stop corpus is a bug to fix, not a marker to delete.
